# Check every text file out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Without this, a clone on a machine with core.autocrlf=true gets CRLF, and the
# build scripts that parse source files — make-sitemap.mjs reading seo.ts is the
# one that bites first — match on patterns like /\n  \{\n/ that CRLF defeats.
# The result is a repository that builds for whoever wrote it and fails for
# everyone else, with an error that blames the file format rather than the
# checkout. The scripts normalise line endings themselves as well; this is the
# half that stops the problem happening in the first place.
#
# text=auto still lets git detect and leave binaries alone; the explicit rules
# below cover the ones that matter here so detection is never the deciding
# factor for a 31 MB wasm or a splash screen.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.wasm  binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
